# --- build and dependency output -------------------------------------------
# `build/` was previously listed here as a generic output pattern, but nothing
# in this repository ever writes to a directory literally named `build` — the
# real compiled output is `dist/`, already covered below. As an unanchored
# pattern, `build/` silently matched `tests/build/` too, which is a real
# source directory (the child-process build tests), not generated output. It
# was never tracked, never committed, and CI's "Child-process build tests"
# step failed with "No test files found" as a result. See A57.
node_modules/
dist/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- generated and diagnostic artifacts -------------------------------------
stress-logs/
graphify-out/
.smart-env/

# --- secrets and local state -------------------------------------------------
# Telga never generates or stores TLS key material, and no .env is used by the
# application. These patterns exist so an accidentally created one cannot be
# published — see `09 Engineering/Local Certificate Handling.md`.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- editor, agent and plugin configuration ---------------------------------
# Personal to this machine, ~19 MB of third-party plugin bundles, and four
# duplicate copies of the same agent skill set. None of it is needed to build,
# test or run Telga.
.obsidian/
.agents/
.claude/
.opencode/
copilot/

# --- commercial and strategic material ---------------------------------------
# Business strategy, provider assessment, engagement records, agreement terms,
# pilot budget and merchant selection. None of it is required by the source,
# tests, build, CI or runtime. Publishing it — even to a private repository — is
# an irreversible disclosure to a third party, and would weaken MuleSoo's
# position before a single agreement exists.
#
# It stays in the vault on this machine. `npm run docs:validate` enforces the
# boundary: a published note that links to one, or names a file inside one, is a
# failure rather than a warning.
docs/obsidian/01 Strategy/
docs/obsidian/06 Partnerships/
docs/obsidian/08 Pilot/
docs/obsidian/00 Home (Local).md

# --- source material and personal workspace files ---------------------------
# The founder's source PDF, and Obsidian's default scratch files.
CLAUDE.pdf
Untitled.canvas
Welcome.md
